# Making landfall from a loaded ship: answer @LANDFALL "Stay With Ships" once, then "Make Landfall" twice.
# Input: output of map_board_and_ferry (Caravel #84 at (48,24) carrying a sentried Colonist #128 and a sentried
# Preacher #131), with the ship's moves refilled and the French goto-order units sentried (orders 1), so no unit
# auto-walks when the selection moves on. The forest tile (47,25) lies south-west of the ship.
key KP_1                   # sail toward the land tile: @LANDFALL popup (Stay With Ships / Make Landfall)
click 150 102              # "Stay With Ships": popup closes, nothing moves, ship still selected
key KP_1                   # same move again: popup again
click 150 114              # "Make Landfall": one passenger (Preacher) goes ashore to (47,25); ship stays at sea; next unit
                           # with moves (Artillery in Quebec) becomes the selection and the view scrolls
click 168 112              # click the ship's tile on the scrolled view: multi-unit stack popup (ship + aboard colonist)
click 120 89               # pick "French Caravel": ship selected again
key KP_1                   # sail toward the land tile once more: @LANDFALL popup
click 150 114              # "Make Landfall": the Colonist goes ashore too; the ship is now empty, selection moves on (to the Artillery
                           # in Quebec again: the hand-off no longer skips it, port_bugs.md #1175a)
